/id #uuid "87e600a5-bf20-5b52-8f26-9ba11cc84dbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-253458" :question/problem "Find the fourth term of the sequence given by the recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n-1}+\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{n-2},\\,{a}_{1}=6,\\,{a}_{2}=3,\\,n\\ge 3.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Starting with the initial terms ${a}_{1}=6,$ and ${a}_{2}=3,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive formula until we reach the fourth term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =6 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =3 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6=\\frac{3}{2}+2=\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ {a}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{3}+\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3=\\frac{7}{4}+1=\\frac{11}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fourth term is ${a}_{4}=\\frac{11}{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-253458/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "516c2e89-2bce-5636-b16d-aa045d9f9c31"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-253458"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-252990"] :question/problem "Find the fifth term of the sequence given by the recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=2{a}_{n-1}-3,\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Starting with the first term ${a}_{1}=5,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive formula until we reach the fifth term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =5 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2{a}_{1}-3=2\\cdot 5-3=7 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =2{a}_{2}-3=2\\cdot 7-3=11 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =2{a}_{3}-3=2\\cdot 11-3=19 \\\\ {a}_{5} & =2{a}_{4}-3=2\\cdot 19-3=35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fifth term is ${a}_{5}=35.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-253349/selection/4e19db70c23a6115ec18a696da26fc333926d5ad3c66f249e5a33cf0b28fc8fa" :answer/id #uuid "10678c62-50b9-5bbe-8b30-666f12e6dce2" :answer/type :answer