{a}_{4} & =3{a}_{3}+2{a}_{2}=3\\cdot 16+2\\cdot 4=48+8=56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fourth term is ${a}_{4}=56.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-253351/selection/ma-v1/b7c1ff80f933b5fae300ae54a01cf20d509914fbd7e102c9dfe248d87301fe0d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-253350/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "96e16b1f-5d30-5b54-be75-811e5c304bf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253350/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "348509c2-a947-5d12-9a2b-c0095156c112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253350/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "412436bd-1d31-549d-8d9a-878b039821b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253350/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "d321f5da-b2c7-5ed5-861e-c578a02c33b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253350/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "e7b8f290-1b9a-5333-bc7b-8a8346a292c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253350/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0519efba-7220-5394-8681-7c287a7b9132" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-253350/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer-field/choices ["q-253350/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-253350/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-253350/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-253350/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" "q-253350/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-253350" :question/id #uuid "9fe8dc59-939f-58df-a247-260dc322c4d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-253350" :question/problem "Find the fourth term of the sequence given by the recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=2{a}_{n-1}-5,\\,{a}_{1}=6,\\,n\\ge 2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Starting with the first term ${a}_{1}=6,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive formula until we reach the fourth term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =6 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2{a}_{1}-5=2\\cdot 6-5=7 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =2{a}_{2}-5=2\\cdot 7-5=9 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =2{a}_{3}-5=2\\cdot 9-5=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fourth term is ${a}_{4}=13.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-253350/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "516c2e89-2bce-5636-b16d-aa045d9f9c31"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-253350"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-253468/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "afe60291-e78e-5362-ba78-9b4c9aea13c0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253468/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "7afe82ec-f00b-5e08-92f9-aea8ca69bc4a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253468/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "d38f5400-d221-566e-ba0f-6a50498ca8ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253468/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "6c37f06d-565a-5a5c-a024-fad7ef60f03e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253468/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "e371e702-80df-5928-a49d-8be0fad5bd09" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253468/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bf99fd1-7c68-5365-8973-de32cc1695e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-253468/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-253468/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-253468/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-253468/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-253468/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-253468/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-253468" :question/id #uuid "21a536a7-eaf5-542f-8447-68faf609e75b" :question/math-academy-id "q-253468" :question/problem "Which of the following recurrence relations are first-order?\n\n- ${a}_{n}={a}_{n-1}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}$\n- ${b}_{n}=3{b}_{n-2}$\n- ${c}_{n}=\\frac{{c}_{n-1}}{3}-2{c}_{n-3}$" :question/worked-solution "The order of a recurrence relation is the largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding terms in the relation.\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- The largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${a}_{n-1}$ in the relation is $1.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $1.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${b}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${b}_{n-1}$ and ${b}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $2.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${c}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${c}_{n-1}$ and ${c}_{n-3}$ in the relation is $3.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-253468/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ade459-9aba-5520-95d3-69ef3fd62d9d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-253468"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-253143"] :question/problem "Which of the following recurrence relations are first-order?\n\n- ${a}_{n}=2{a}_{n-2}$\n- ${b}_{n}={b}_{n-1}^{2}+2{b}_{n-2}$\n- ${c}_{n}=2{c}_{n-1}+n$" :question/worked-solution "The order of a recurrence relation is the largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding terms in the relation.\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- The largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${a}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $2.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${b}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${b}_{n-1}$ and ${b}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $2.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${c}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${c}_{n-1}$ in the relation is $1.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-253467/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "dfd9e09c-3af1-5357-a194-5ad2d142ec4e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253467/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "23280fef-78ec-549d-bcaa-c6e571df17e6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253467/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "42c55047-f997-5ea6-bd36-4da4ac949992" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253467/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "bcb47e66-f818-55d0-8acd-af323ae32217" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253467/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "e15733f7-a966-55ef-bb08-6687b8f6f821" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253467/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3c7aabb-6f2a-5ed2-8170-e3cf7fa1d02a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-253467/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-253467/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-253467/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-253467/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-253467/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-253467/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-253467" :question/id #uuid "5fa8f043-0108-5d57-9b6a-3ff01feefed4" :question/math-academy-id "q-253467" :question/problem "Which of the following recurrence relations are first-order?\n\n- ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{a}_{n-2}}{2}+3$\n- ${b}_{n}=2{b}_{n-1}-{b}_{n-2}$\n- ${c}_{n}={c}_{n-1}+\\frac{1}{3}$" :question/worked-solution "The order of a recurrence relation is the largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding terms in the relation.\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- The largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${a}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $2.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${b}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${b}_{n-1}$ and ${b}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $2.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${c}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${c}_{n-1}$ in the relation is $1.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-253467/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ade459-9aba-5520-95d3-69ef3fd62d9d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-253467"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-253144/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "04117c07-cab8-5239-966a-b01e9b7ec735" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253144/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "bf61f159-fabf-5cb6-8bcf-f4d03c42ef03" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253144/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "acfd1a4b-8a3a-578c-9b26-541bc83beeb4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253144/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "006c188d-38c8-5e26-a134-a13fb7cefd5c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253144/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "873f2c05-12cf-5210-962f-d1c4ebe188a9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253144/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "040ccf82-071a-5447-bab7-f9a303883c5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-253144/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-253144/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-253144/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-253144/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-253144/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-253144/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-253144" :question/id #uuid "6af1f1dd-0830-5336-97d9-6d826a433e28" :question/math-academy-id "q-253144" :question/problem "Which of the following linear recurrence relations are homogeneous?\n\n- ${a}_{n}=2{a}_{n-1}+5{a}_{n-2}$\n- ${b}_{n}={b}_{n-1}+3{b}_{n-2}$\n- ${c}_{n}=4{c}_{n-1}+7n$" :question/worked-solution "A linear recurrence relation (with constant coefficients) is **homogeneous** if the forcing function is zero. \n\nIn other words, the linear recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={s}_{1}{a}_{n-1}+{s}_{2}{a}_{n-2}+…+{s}_{k}{a}_{n-k}+g(n),\n$$\n\nis homogeneous if $g(n)=0$ for all $n,$ and ${s}_{i}$ is constant for each $i.$\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- ${a}_{n}$ is homogeneous. The terms of the expression each contain a preceding term, ${a}_{n-1}$ and ${a}_{n-2}.$\n\n- ${b}_{n}$ is homogeneous. The terms of the expression each contain a preceding term, ${b}_{n-1}$ and ${b}_{n-2}.$\n\n- ${c}_{n}$ is not homogeneous. The term $7n$ of the expression doesn't contain preceding terms of the relation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-253144/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ade459-9aba-5520-95d3-69ef3fd62d9d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-253144"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-253485/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "9084c9f5-8844-5530-96c0-ead88cd2759f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253485/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "15d6f5e5-a822-5ab0-b237-a155e9613033" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253485/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "b690c061-d802-51db-b28e-bd26f6757e44" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253485/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "f1269aed-048a-5327-ba68-e236ed687459" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253485/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "b00fbc66-decb-5218-94b4-c50b9abb3a53" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253485/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d519759-a179-55ef-8eb8-921a715ea0a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-253485/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-253485/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-253485/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-253485/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-253485/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-253485/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-253485" :question/id #uuid "40a9896d-2592-5ccb-afef-6c9ca025eef5" :question/math-academy-id "q-253485" :question/problem "Which of the following linear recurrence relations are homogeneous?\n\n- ${a}_{n}=3{a}_{n-1}+2{a}_{n-2}$\n- ${b}_{n}=4{b}_{n-1}+{n}^{2}$\n- ${c}_{n}=5{c}_{n-1}+6{c}_{n-2}$" :question/worked-solution "A linear recurrence relation (with constant coefficients) is **homogeneous** if the forcing function is zero. \n\nIn other words, the linear recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={s}_{1}{a}_{n-1}+{s}_{2}{a}_{n-2}+…+{s}_{k}{a}_{n-k}+g(n),\n$$\n\nis homogeneous if $g(n)=0$ for all $n,$ and ${s}_{i}$ is constant for each $i.$\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- ${a}_{n}$ is homogeneous. The terms of the expression each contain a preceding term, ${a}_{n-1}$ and ${a}_{n-2}.$\n\n- ${b}_{n}$ is not homogeneous. The term ${n}^{2}$ of the expression doesn't contain preceding terms of the relation.\n\n- ${c}_{n}$ is homogeneous. The terms of the expression each contain a preceding term, ${c}_{n-1}$ and ${c}_{n-2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-253485/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ade459-9aba-5520-95d3-69ef3fd62d9d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-253485"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-253362/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "bcaceabd-e8d3-596b-9a56-33eefe1d4661" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253362/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "21f6bead-4306-5ced-b37f-0a8a83f20b5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-253362/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77